# A definition takes a single decorator list: `@[a, b, c]` already applies
# several decorators, left to right, so a second list stacked on the first
# (`@[a]` then `@[b]`) is a syntax error. A class body reaches the same check
# (ParseDecorator); the module form is the one exercised here.
#
# Today the error is reported through the COMP-001 assert in file mode; the
# message is checked, not the way the process exits.
#
# EXPECT: error: Invalid decorator placement

func d(f) { return f }

@[d]
@[d]
func twice_listed() { return 1 }
